⍝ lib/real.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 8: more of analysis on the lazy ℝ[i]
⍝ (every function returns a stream of exact ℚ[i] approximants; where a convergence modulus is known it is stated)
⍝ ---- pointwise operations on streams
÷ᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ → ℝ
÷ᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
÷ᴿ ≔ (⫴ ÷)
ℜᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ
ℜᴿ ≔ (⫶ ℜ)
ℑᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ
ℑᴿ ≔ (⫶ ℑ)
⍝ pointwise integer power of a lazy number: element n of x^k is (element n of x)^k
^ᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℤ → ℝ   ⍝ pointwise integer power of a lazy number
^ᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℤ → ℝ[i]
^ᴿ ξ η ≔ (⫶ (θ ↦ (^ θ η)) ξ)
⍝ the diagonal: element n of (⟐ f x) is element n of f(xₙ).  It extends a function of ℚ[i] with approximants f to the lazy ℝ[i]
⍝ (it converges to f(x) when f is continuous at x).
⟐′ ∶ (α → 𝔖 β) → 𝔖 α → 𝔇 → 𝔖 β
⟐′ ξ η ν ≔ (∷ (hd (drop′ ν (ξ (hd η)))) (⟐′ ξ (⌄ η) (⊞ᶻ ν (◀ 1))))
⟐ ∶ (α → 𝔖 β) → 𝔖 α → 𝔖 β
⟐ ξ η ≔ (⟐′ ξ η ⊥)
⍝ ---- square roots.  For x ≥ 0 in ℚ, element n of √x is ⌊√(x·4ⁿ)⌋ / 2ⁿ: it is within 2⁻ⁿ of √x, from below (a modulus of convergence).
⍝ For z = a + bi the principal root is √((|z| + a)/2) + i·sgn(b)·√((|z| − a)/2), with |z| taken from the same stream index.
sq⁺ ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℚ
sq⁺ ξ θ ≔ (÷ (isqrt (⌊ (⊠ ξ (⊠ θ θ)))) θ)
√⁺′ ∶ ℚ → ℚ → 𝔖 ℚ
√⁺′ ξ θ ≔ (∷ (sq⁺ ξ θ) (√⁺′ ξ (⊠ θ 1100)))
√ᶜ′ ∶ ℚ → ℚ → 𝔖 ℚ → ℚ → 𝔖 ℚ[i]
√ᶜ′ ϕ ψ ρ θ ≔ (∷ (⊞ (sq⁺ (÷ (⊞ (hd ρ) ϕ) 1100) θ) (⊠ ((⩾ ψ 0) 11 111) (sq⁺ (÷ (⊟ (hd ρ) ϕ) 1100) θ))) (√ᶜ′ ϕ ψ (⌄ ρ) (⊠ θ 1100)))
√ ∶ ℚ → ℝ
√ ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
√ ξ ≔ ((ϕ ψ ↦ ((∧ (≐ ψ 0) (⩾ ϕ 0)) (√⁺′ ϕ 1) (√ᶜ′ ϕ ψ (√⁺′ (⊞ (⊠ ϕ ϕ) (⊠ ψ ψ)) 1) 1))) (ℜ ξ) (ℑ ξ))
⍝ ---- logarithm: log x = 2·artanh y = 2 Σ y^(2k+1)/(2k+1),  y = (x − 1)/(x + 1);  converges for x > 0 (for z ∈ ℚ[i]: Re z > 0, principal branch)
log ∶ ℚ → ℝ
log ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
log ξ ≔ ((υ ↦ (Σ (⊠ 1100 υ) (ς ↦ (÷ (⊠ (⊠ υ υ) (⊟ (⊠ 1100 ς) 1)) (⊞ (⊠ 1100 ς) 1))))) (÷ (⊟ ξ 1) (⊞ ξ 1)))
⍝ ---- arctangent by Euler's series  atan x = Σ 2²ᵏ(k!)²/(2k+1)! · x^(2k+1)/(1 + x²)^(k+1):  ratio (2k/(2k+1))·x²/(1 + x²) < 1, so it
⍝ converges for every real x (at x = 1 it is the series of π/4 used by the π of examples/target)
atan ∶ ℚ → ℝ
atan ξ ≔ ((ω ↦ (Σ (÷ ξ ω) (ς ↦ (÷ (⊠ (⊠ 1100 ς) (⊠ ξ ξ)) (⊠ (⊞ (⊠ 1100 ς) 1) ω))))) (⊞ 1 (⊠ ξ ξ)))
⍝ ---- hyperbolic functions and tangents
sinh ∶ ℚ → ℝ
sinh ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
sinh ξ ≔ (Σ ξ (ς ↦ (÷ (⊠ ξ ξ) (⊠ (⊠ 1100 ς) (⊞ (⊠ 1100 ς) 1)))))
cosh ∶ ℚ → ℝ
cosh ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
cosh ξ ≔ (Σ 1 (ς ↦ (÷ (⊠ ξ ξ) (⊠ (⊟ (⊠ 1100 ς) 1) (⊠ 1100 ς)))))
tan ∶ ℚ → ℝ
tan ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
tan ξ ≔ (÷ᴿ (sin ξ) (cos ξ))
tanh ∶ ℚ → ℝ
tanh ∶ ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
tanh ξ ≔ (÷ᴿ (sinh ξ) (cosh ξ))
⍝ ---- the same functions of a lazy argument (through the diagonal)
expᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ
expᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
expᴿ ≔ (⟐ exp)
sinᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ
sinᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
sinᴿ ≔ (⟐ sin)
cosᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ
cosᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
cosᴿ ≔ (⟐ cos)
√ᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ
√ᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ[i]
√ᴿ ≔ (⟐ √)
logᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ
logᴿ ≔ (⟐ log)
atanᴿ ∶ ℝ → ℝ
atanᴿ ≔ (⟐ atan)
⍝ |z| of a lazy complex number, and the absolute value of a lazy real
absᴿ ∶ ℝ[i] → ℝ
absᴿ ξ ≔ (√ᴿ (⫶ 𝒩 ξ))
⍝ ---- derivative and integral as streams.  ∂ f x: central difference quotients with h = 2⁻ⁿ (error O(h²) for f of class C³);
⍝ ∫ f a b: element n is the midpoint rule with n + 1 equal parts (converges for continuous f)
∂′ ∶ (ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]) → ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → 𝔖 ℚ[i]
∂′ φ ξ η ≔ (∷ (÷ (⊟ (φ (⊞ ξ η)) (φ (⊟ ξ η))) (⊠ 1100 η)) (∂′ φ ξ (÷ η 1100)))
∂ ∶ (ℚ → ℚ) → ℚ → ℝ
∂ ∶ (ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]) → ℚ[i] → ℝ[i]
∂ φ ξ ≔ (∂′ φ ξ 1)
mid′ ∶ (ℚ → ℚ) → ℚ → ℚ → ℕ → ℚ
mid′ φ ξ ζ ν ≔ (⊠ ζ (sumof (⫶ (κ ↦ (φ (⊞ ξ (⊠ (⊞ κ 1.11) ζ)))) (⍳ ν))))
∫ ∶ (ℚ → ℚ) → ℚ → ℚ → ℝ
∫ φ ξ η ≔ (⫶ (ν ↦ (mid′ φ ξ (÷ (⊟ η ξ) ν) ν)) (iterate (ν ↦ (⊞ ν 1)) 1))
